[Music]  37 year old leo who prefers using a  pseudonym for privacy reasons  was a marketing director at an internet  startup in beijing  until she got pregnant in 2017  on the second day after i learned that i  was pregnant i told the company about  the situation  in two days the company sent me on a  business trip to shanghai and shenzhen  for about a week  when i came back from the business trip  i found out the company had recruited  the appropriate candidate for my  position who would be employed shortly  after hiring a candidate for this  position they demoted me  and dismissed me stopped paying my  salary and closed my work mailbox  she is still deep in a legal battle to  win her unpaid salary and an apology  from the company  my first appeal was a labour arbitration  in 2017 for labour disputes  from 2017 to 2021 it has been more than  four years  nearly five years i think this process  has been very long and torturous  leo is part of growing gender  discrimination in the workplace in china  a side effect of beijing's push to boost  birth rates  although there are no official  statistics lawyers and labor activists  say there's been a notable pickup in  cases of employers declining to give  jobs and promotions to women since  china's one child policy officially  ended in 2016.  currently chinese women make up 40  of the total labor force however women  face a big  big glass selling when they try to climb  climb up the  corporate ladder and at the hiring stage  women are also facing difficulties when  job posting explicitly or implicitly say  that  they prefer men over women to address  the problem the government in 2019  laid out more specific rules to ban  discriminatory practices in the hiring  process  even though china has one of the highest  female labor force participation rates  in asia  women there are still expected to be the  primary caregiver of children due to the  lack of child care services  another thing is women currently needs  to sacrifice their own career to  give birth to baby china is very special  in a sense that  it provides very extensive maternity  belief to mother  well it does not provide any states a  national level parental before father  that means  when when a woman decides to be a mom  she will need to take months away from  work and she when she come back she may  only face  more discrimination than before  in leo's case a beijing court ruled in  favor of the company in december  and rejected her appeal earlier this  month  the court accepted the company's  argument that each of its actions was a  normal business decision  and decided there was not enough  evidence to prove discriminatory  intentions  but she remains hopeful  now our country has opened up to three  children and announced that we will also  support the protection of three children  with corresponding protective measures  this will include the protection of  women's rights so i think in the future  there will be more policies and  regulations protecting the rights and  interests of our women  you

